# Code owners for HyFib Tailor360.
#
# The last pattern that matches a file decides its owners, so the broad rule comes first and the
# tighter rules follow it. Owners listed here are requested for review automatically, and — once
# branch protection requires a review from a code owner — a pull request touching those paths
# cannot merge without one.
#
# PLACEHOLDER HANDLES. `@MK-AIFy/tailor360-maintainers` and `@MK-AIFy/tailor360-platform` do not
# exist yet. The repository owner replaces both with the real handles before enabling code-owner
# review:
#   * an organisation-owned repository uses team handles (`@org/team`), and the team must have
#     write access to this repository or GitHub ignores the entry;
#   * a personally owned repository cannot use team handles at all — use the personal handle
#     (`@MK-AIFy`) on every line instead, otherwise GitHub reports the file as invalid and applies
#     none of it.

# Everything, unless a tighter rule below claims it.
*                       @MK-AIFy/tailor360-maintainers

# Deployment topology, compose stacks, Dockerfiles and the reverse proxy: a change here can expose
# a port, weaken a container or break the migrate-before-serve ordering, and none of that shows up
# in a test.
/infra/                 @MK-AIFy/tailor360-platform

# Workflows, governance and repository policy. A workflow change can alter what CI is allowed to do
# with the workflow token, so it is reviewed by the same people who own the deployment.
/.github/               @MK-AIFy/tailor360-platform

# Architecture decision records: an ADR is the record of a decision that binds every later issue,
# so it is not amended in passing.
/docs/adr/              @MK-AIFy/tailor360-platform

# The shared kernel. Every module depends on it, so a change here is a change to all of them.
/src/Platform/          @MK-AIFy/tailor360-platform
